---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('attentive')!;
const path = '/apps/attentive';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/attentive');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/attentive');

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is Attentive worth it for a Shopify store doing $80k per month?',
    answer: 'Assess the actual quote, expected eligible send volume, margin and staffing rather than monthly store revenue alone. An $80k store can compare Attentive with Postscript or Omnisend using the same channel scope and support requirements; no merchant test or universal revenue cutoff is established here.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How does Attentive pricing compare to Postscript on Shopify?',
    answer: 'Obtain current written quotes for identical countries, SMS segments, carrier fees, email volume, onboarding, services and contract term. A Shopify installation price is not the total messaging bill. Confirm minimums and renewal terms directly; this review does not establish a typical contract range or a lower-cost winner.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does Attentive include email for Shopify stores?',
    answer: 'Yes. The official Shopify listing describes both email and SMS. Confirm the particular journeys, integrations and services included in your proposed plan; running another email provider alongside it requires explicit sender and suppression ownership.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is Attentive two-tap opt-in for Shopify mobile traffic?',
    answer: 'Two-tap signup is an SMS acquisition flow advertised in the official Shopify listing. Evaluate it on the actual mobile storefront with clear channel-specific permission and retained consent records. A signup interaction does not itself establish legal compliance or a comparative conversion advantage.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does Attentive implementation take on Shopify?',
    answer: 'Plan rollout around consent review, creative approval, event mapping, integration QA and a staged cutover. Ask for a written implementation scope and owner for each task. No standard four-to-twelve-week delivery period is established here; avoid overlapping migrations unless the team can validate both safely.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Attentive vs Klaviyo for scaled Shopify brands?',
    answer: 'Compare the email and SMS workflows your store needs, supported Shopify events, reporting, support commitments and full costs in a scoped pilot. Neither a universal data-depth winner nor a support SLA is established by this review. A split stack requires explicit ownership of each send.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the biggest Attentive mistake enterprise merchants make?',
    answer: 'Committing before defining how incremental contribution will be measured. Attributed revenue can overlap across email and SMS. Where feasible, use randomized eligible cohorts with consistent windows, account for returns and messaging costs, and distinguish attribution from causal lift before renewal.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Who should skip Attentive entirely?',
    answer: 'Teams that cannot fund the quoted scope or maintain consent, suppression, creative approvals and reporting should reconsider the rollout. Compare simpler alternatives against the same requirements; store revenue alone does not establish suitability.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/apps" class="text-sm font-bold text-[#9a5b16] hover:text-[#24170f]">← All tool reviews</a>
      <p class="catalog-kicker mt-6">Email, SMS and operating scope</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Attentive markets email and SMS for ecommerce, including two-tap signup units in its official Shopify listing. Evaluate acquisition, journey controls and the services in your actual quote against your team capacity. Confirm send-time features and onboarding responsibilities directly; store revenue alone is not a reliable eligibility threshold.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#5d3a1d]">Illustrative evaluation cases below use a specialty tea brand with pop-up retail, a mechanical keyboard house planning 12k daily launch sends, and a climbing gear company assessing a larger messaging contract. These are planning scenarios, not merchant tests or documented results.</p>
      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript review</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo review</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <TldrBox
      title="Verdict: Attentive for Shopify"
      picks={[
        { label: 'Positioning', tool: 'Email and SMS', reason: 'Evaluate channels and contracted operator support separately.' },
        { label: 'Pricing', tool: 'Custom contracts', reason: 'Request a scoped quote including usage, fees and services.' },
        { label: 'Strength', tool: 'Two-tap opt-in', reason: 'Mobile acquisition UX for Instagram/TikTok traffic at scale.' },
        { label: 'Tradeoff', tool: 'Implementation time', reason: 'Agree an implementation schedule after mapping integration and approval work.' },
        { label: 'Best for', tool: 'Staffed DTC programs', reason: 'SMS as board metric with compliance and creative teams.' },
      ]}
    />

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">When to evaluate a managed SMS program</h2>
      <p>Multi-brand portfolios, international permission requirements, rapid creative production and executive reporting can make a managed SMS program worth evaluating. Ask Attentive and Postscript to demonstrate the same event triggers, review process and support escalation. Confirm which growth services and optimization features are included instead of assuming a platform ceiling.</p>
      <p>For an illustrative $2.1M/mo keyboard brand planning 12k daily launch sends, model legal review and creative capacity alongside software cost. For a $400k/mo climbing shop, compare quotes against margin from eligible recovery opportunities. Neither scenario establishes comparative recovery lift or a preferred supplier.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-[#24170f]">1. Two-tap opt-in — tea pop-up retail</h3>
      <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> Pop-up booth QR to mobile storefront. <strong>Attentive setup:</strong> Two-tap flow with compliance copy reviewed by legal.</p>
      <p><strong>Proposed measurement:</strong> Compare eligible mobile visitors randomly assigned to signup variants, recording valid channel permission and completed opt-ins. No 41% versus 28% result has been established; evaluate acquisition quality and subsequent unsubscribes as well as signup rate.</p>
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-[#24170f]">2. Drop-week orchestration — keyboards</h3>
      <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> Limited switch drop, VIP SMS early access. <strong>Setup:</strong> Coordinated with Klaviyo email suppression and holdout group.</p>
      <p><strong>Proposed measurement:</strong> Randomize eligible VIPs between coordinated email-plus-SMS and email-only cohorts. Compare net contribution over the same window, including returns and message costs; no 8.2% lift is established here.</p>
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-[#24170f]">3. Cross-channel journey — climbing gear</h3>
      <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> Browse abandon SMS, email follow-up, concierge reply for $400+ harness carts. <strong>Setup:</strong> Attentive journey with two-way routing rules.</p>
      <p><strong>Proposed measurement:</strong> For assisted $400+ carts, separate conversation-assisted attributed sales from causal lift. Verify reply routing, staff coverage, fresh purchase state and consent before each follow-up. No 22% recovery outcome is established.</p>
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-[#24170f]">4. Rejected fit — $400k/mo gear shop</h3>
      <p><strong>Illustrative scenario:</strong> A $400k/mo gear shop compares written Attentive and Postscript quotes for identical traffic, countries, segments and service scope. <strong>Decision:</strong> Finance checks total fees and staffing against expected contribution; the previous $900 and $220 amounts were not verified quotes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 mb-12">
      <div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Pros</p><ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">{['Email and SMS journeys and shared audiences are supplier-described capabilities.', 'Two-tap signup is described in the Shopify listing.'].map((s) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">+</span>{s}</li>)}</ul></div>
      <div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Cons</p><ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">{['Installation cost does not establish the full messaging bill.', 'Service deliverables and account responsibilities require a scoped agreement.'].map((l) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">−</span>{l}</li>)}</ul></div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Attentive operating discipline on Shopify</h2>
      <p>Define incrementality before renewal. In the proposed keyboard launch, an email-only holdout can help estimate the extra contribution from SMS; for tea pop-ups, measure valid opt-ins separately from sends. Attributed revenue is a reporting convention and does not establish what would have happened without the message.</p>
      <p>Fit legal and creative review into the drop calendar. Agree lead times and emergency approval owners with the supplier rather than assuming a four-week requirement. Platform controls can assist operations but do not guarantee compliant messages; validate purpose, audience permission, quiet-hour settings and the approved copy.</p>
      <p>If Klaviyo email and Attentive SMS coexist, document permission separately by channel, frequency caps, VIP definitions and supported event mappings. A Shopify tag is not proof of consent. Assign one owner per journey, recheck purchase and suppression state before a queued send, and deduplicate replayed events; consolidation needs the same validation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Illustrative stack patterns to evaluate with Attentive</h2>
      <p><strong>Illustrative $2.1M/mo specialty tea:</strong> Evaluate mobile signup at pop-ups with Klaviyo email lifecycle and a shared VIP definition. Verify integration mapping and permission records separately. SMS acquisition and email replenishment need distinct send owners and a common collision policy.</p>
      <p><strong>Illustrative keyboard launches:</strong> Consider SMS early access for opted-in VIPs and a coordinated email offer window. Confirm suppression actually reaches queued sends, define an expiry time for access and plan a randomized comparison if volume supports it.</p>
      <p><strong>Illustrative $400k/mo climbing gear:</strong> Compare an SMS specialist with the proposed Attentive service package. Finance should include staff time, carrier fees, peak launch volume and termination terms; no rejected quote or cheaper equivalent outcome is documented here.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-12">
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg font-bold">
        <li><a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- EXPANSION_BLOCK_v2 -->

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Attentive in a three-layer Shopify stack</h2>
      <p>Attentive fits brands with traffic economics that justify premium SMS programs and managed growth support.</p>
      <p>Attentive markets email and SMS together. Compare a consolidated account with a split email/SMS stack using the same journeys and audiences. Neither architecture makes Shopify order notifications, service replies or marketing permission interchangeable. Record those responsibilities before selecting the channel plan.</p>
      
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="ledger-card">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">Evaluation checklist</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Score Attentive on your Shopify store</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">
        
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Can your team maintain flows monthly without agency dependency?</li>
        
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Will finance trust revenue attribution without custom BI?</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Does SMS/email/push suppression integrate or require manual tags?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- EXPANSION_BLOCK_v3 -->

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Attentive migration and co-existence</h2>
      <p>A proposed fragrance merchant can compare retaining Attentive email and SMS with separating the channels. Inventory active templates, integrations, account access and operator work before pricing the alternative. A vinyl label can instead rehearse its allocation segments in the existing account. Neither exercise establishes a supplier switch, labor saving or segmentation winner.</p>
      <p>Stage cart and welcome migration using test profiles and mutually exclusive eligible cohorts. Assign one active sender for each customer and journey, preserve channel permission and suppressions, deduplicate event replays and cancel stale queued sends after purchase. Set rollback criteria before cutover; do not use dual promotional sends or matching attributed totals as proof of correctness.</p>
      <p>When Attentive pairs with Postscript SMS, Privy capture or AfterShip event tooling, document which product owns each message, event and permission record. Two SMS providers must not independently target the same cart. Confirm event availability, current purchase state and queue cancellation across integrations before launch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- TARGETED_EXPANSION_v4 -->

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Enterprise SMS when traffic economics justify Attentive</h2>
      <p>In an illustrative $2M/mo apparel launch, compare a managed contract against internal staffing and software-only alternatives. Record the proposed creative deliverables and onboarding milestones. Neither a $2,800 contract, an 18% revenue contribution, a 40% list increase nor a four-week implementation was verified; use measured pilot data and actual quotes.</p>
      <p>Compare the service package against the work your team will actually use: campaign planning, template changes, approval handling and reporting. Ask who performs each task and how requests are escalated. Monthly store revenue does not establish an email eligibility limit or a cost-equivalent alternative.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- TARGETED_EXPANSION_v5 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Checkout opt-in</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Two-tap at scale</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">For a proposed apparel mobile signup evaluation, record eligible visitors, permission completion and later opt-outs. Confirm whether the placement is supported on the actual storefront and checkout plan. Ask who reviews consent language and what the contracted service includes; no 40% uplift or comparative legal-hours saving is established.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v6 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Attentive email plus SMS orchestration</h2><p>Attentive markets a dedicated email product with a no-code builder, shared audiences and cross-channel journeys. For a proposed apparel drop, build an email-only version as well as a coordinated email/SMS journey. Check rendering, audience exclusions, offer expiry and purchase exits; do not infer email depth or relative price from historic SMS positioning.</p><p>If the quote includes BFCM scripts and MMS assets, specify deliverables, revision rounds and approval ownership. Compare their replacement cost only when the team would otherwise purchase or perform that work. Confirm whether a software-only alternative meets the same launch requirements.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v7 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Benchmark</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Attentive vs Postscript: a proposed $1M/mo scenario</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">For an illustrative $1M/mo beauty brand, compare Attentive and Postscript on mutually exclusive eligible cohorts with identical offers and windows. Include message segments, carrier fees, creative services and internal labor in both costs. No 6.2% versus 6.8% recovery test, $1,400 versus $2,600 bill or later supplier switch is documented; require evidence before drawing a winner.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v8 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="ledger-card"><p class="catalog-kicker">List growth</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">List growth compliance review</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">Ask whether the proposed service includes consent-copy review, which jurisdictions it covers and who retains legal responsibility. Obtain written deliverables rather than assuming state-specific appendices or external counsel savings. Compare legal and operational costs only for equivalent scope.</p></div></section>

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Enterprise SMS when minimums clear ROI hurdle</h2>
      <p>Evaluate managed onboarding and creative services against the needs of climbing-gear flash sales and vinyl allocation alerts. Verify every quoted service. SMS-attributed GMV alone cannot justify a minimum: compare incremental contribution, returns and total costs, and test whether an internal owner can maintain an alternative safely.</p>
      <p><strong>Proposed outdoor-gear service review.</strong> Inventory which contracted deliverables were used and which the team could maintain internally. Have the replacement operator edit, approve and pause a real draft before ending services. Compare actual workload and contribution without asserting equal ROI or a percentage saving.</p>
      <p><strong>Illustrative beauty launch with legal exposure.</strong> Ask what jurisdiction-specific consent review is included and estimate any avoided external work from actual scope. No reduction in counsel hours is established; supplier documentation does not transfer merchant responsibility.</p>
      <h2>Buyer checklist</h2>
      <ul><li>Incremental contribution supports total messaging and service costs?</li><li>Creative services actually used — not line item guilt?</li><li>Internal owner assigned before downshift — concierge does not maintain flows post-launch?</li>        <li>Self-serve edit drill passed before first post-exit drop?</li></ul>
      <p>Review stack fit quarterly using total costs, service use and incremental contribution. Unused creative services may motivate renegotiation, but a cheaper subscription does not establish equivalent outcomes. Validate replacement workflows and staff capacity before ending the existing arrangement.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Enterprise versus SMB SMS economics</h2>
      <p>For an illustrative sub-800-order climbing shop, compare contract minimums with reachable, permissioned audiences and expected contribution from flash drops. There is no documented switch with equal recovery, 41% lower cost or thirty-minute weekly workload; measure the replacement on its actual scope.</p>
      <p>Creative services have replacement cost only if used — unused concierge line item is exit signal. Self-serve edit drill before first post-exit drop: if Thursday allocation SMS requires ticket queue on replacement stack, downshift failed regardless of subscription delta.</p>
      <p>For migration, retain the provenance, wording, timestamps and channel scope of permission records and preserve revocations. Have the responsible reviewer assess the actual jurisdiction and campaign purpose; there is no universal 50k-subscriber legal-review threshold. Use a controlled cutover with no overlapping promotional sender ownership.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">90-day enterprise SMS proof plan</h2>
      <p>Illustrative 90-day plan: week one maps quoted minimums, usage and measurement; week two validates candidate quiet hours with test profiles; week three assigns an operator and measures the real workload. Week four can pilot a flash drop with an eligible holdout. Weeks five through twelve audit service use and full costs. Decide only when evidence supports the comparison; ninety days does not guarantee sufficient sample size.</p>
      <p>For a planned vinyl drop to eight thousand eligible SMS subscribers, model peak segments and carrier fees separately. Ask whether consent-review appendices are included and estimate legal-work costs from actual deliverables. Neither a legal-hours saving nor guaranteed compliance is established.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-bold">
      <a class="link" href="/apps">All Shopify email tools →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/alternatives/attentive-alternative">Attentive alternatives →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

    <h2>Attentive buyer desk: enterprise SMS orchestration</h2>
    <p>For a proposed enterprise evaluation, separate channel choice from service choice. A pottery waitlist may need SMS for an available seat and email for the syllabus; a coffee subscription may need educational email and an optional reminder. Demonstrate both in the selected account. Decide whether the internal operator or contracted team owns copy, audience changes, scheduling and emergency pause. Record a measurable acceptance criterion for each task before renewal; no ninety-day lift or complaint outcome is promised.</p>

    <h2>Attentive operator: cross-channel QA ritual</h2>
    <p>Before each major promotion, use authorized staff test profiles to validate cart events, channel permission, quiet hours, purchase cancellation and cross-provider suppression. Record failures with an owner. For climbing and outdoor launches, check MMS rendering on representative devices and carriers. For coffee subscriptions, test opt-in and revocation records separately from device notification settings. Report attributed revenue separately from any randomized incremental-lift estimate.</p>

    <p>Make unresolved permission, stale purchase-state or duplicate-send failures launch blocking. Keep the QA record and fix owner for each issue before the next send window. This is an operating recommendation, not evidence of observed complaint spikes or a completed merchant test.</p>

<section class="container py-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Account control and service acceptance</h2><p>Checked November 25, 2026: the <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/attentive">active Shopify listing</a> describes email, SMS, two-tap signup and automation. <a href="https://www.attentive.com/email-marketing">Attentive email documentation</a> describes a builder, shared audiences, journeys and migration support. These establish marketed scope, not the deliverables included in a particular agreement.</p><p>For an enterprise pilot, identify the merchant administrator, billing owner and staff allowed to publish or pause messages. Ask for the contracted scope of migration, creative work and support, including exclusions and escalation. The merchant needs a usable operating path when an agency contact is absent or a service engagement ends.</p><p>Have the actual operator create an email draft, edit an SMS offer, preview both, obtain approval and cancel a scheduled test. Confirm whether a service ticket is needed for any step. Record completion time and blockers without substituting a supplier demo for operator acceptance.</p><p>Before consolidating email, inventory the sending domain, authentication, templates, audience definitions and suppression records. Confirm the proposed warm-up and cutover responsibilities with the supplier. Test an email revocation with an SMS opt-in still active and the reverse; a shared profile must retain those distinct states. For a split stack, demonstrate the integration rather than assuming a shared identifier provides automatic collision control.</p><p>Review an illustrative launch invoice using the same subscriber population and planned messages under each quote. Separate software, usage, carrier charges, onboarding and optional services; then add internal review and reply work. Obtain notice, export and account-access terms before deciding whether to retain, consolidate or replace channels.</p></div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Attentive Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
